Package: agriGrowthFlow
Type: Package
Title: Design-Aware Plant Growth and Longitudinal Trajectory Analysis
Version: 1.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Walter Esfrain", "Pereira", email = "wep@cca.ufpb.br", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1085-0191")),
    person("Magali Haidee", "Pereira Martinez", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-5419-959X"))
  )
Description: Provides a design-aware workflow for plant growth analysis. The
    foundational layer validates destructive and repeated sampling structures and
    calculates classical growth indices, biomass partitioning, and allometry. The
    parametric layer fits biologically interpretable nonlinear growth curves with
    guarded initialization, diagnostics, prediction, and derived traits. The
    longitudinal and flexible layer adds mixed-effects growth-curve analysis,
    explicit residual correlation and variance structures, smoothing splines,
    LOESS, generalized additive and shape-constrained additive trajectories,
    first and second derivatives, functional principal component analysis, and
    multivariate comparison of orthogonal growth components. The uncertainty
    layer adds design-aware bootstrap resampling, bootstrap confidence intervals,
    model-selection stability, Bayesian nonlinear hierarchical growth models,
    prior and posterior predictive checks, posterior growth-trait uncertainty,
    MCMC diagnostics, Pareto-smoothed leave-one-out evaluation, and stacking or
    pseudo-BMA model weighting. The biological-events and decisions layer adds
    ordered multiphase logistic trajectories, numerical stability points, exploratory
    changepoints, measured biomass-loss events, iterative defoliation analysis,
    compensatory-growth summaries, density and neighborhood competition tools,
    coupled logistic competition simulations, biologically defined thresholds and
    plateaus, model-conditioned harvest optimization, observation-schedule heuristics,
    design simulation, and Monte Carlo power for derived growth traits. The
    consolidated release adds design-aware method guidance, auditable workflow
    orchestration, standardized result tables, Markdown reporting, and reproducible
    export bundles while preserving access to all specialist modules. Methods preserve
    the persistent experimental unit and do not treat destructive subsamples as
    independent longitudinal individuals.
